Full API spec:
All Java classes are in the default package (no package declarations). Public API and semantics:

src/main/java/Direction.java: public enum Direction { LEFT, RIGHT, UP, DOWN }
- Used by Board.move(Direction) and Game.move(Direction).

src/main/java/MoveResult.java:
- public final class MoveResult { public MoveResult(boolean changed, int scoreGained); public boolean changed(); public int scoreGained(); }
- Immutable: fields set at construction and never change. changed() indicates whether any grid cell changed. scoreGained() sums all newly created tile values from merges performed by that single move.

src/main/java/Spawn.java:
- public final class Spawn { public Spawn(int row, int col, int value); public int row(); public int col(); public int value(); }
- Constructor validates: 0 <= row < 4, 0 <= col < 4, value > 0 and a power of two (e.g., 2,4,8,...). Immutable.

src/main/java/Spawner.java:
- public interface Spawner { Spawn nextSpawn(); }
- Contract: Deterministic source. Game consumes exactly two spawns during reset() and exactly one spawn after a changed move. Implementations must not return null.

src/main/java/SequenceSpawner.java:
- public final class SequenceSpawner implements Spawner { public SequenceSpawner(java.util.List<Spawn> seq); public Spawn nextSpawn(); public static SequenceSpawner defaultSequence(); }
- Holds an ordered sequence of Spawn. nextSpawn() returns sequence[index] and advances index; when reaching end, wraps to start and continues. defaultSequence() returns a deterministic spawner with a documented sequence; the first two spawns are used by Game.reset().

src/main/java/GameStatus.java:
- public enum GameStatus { IN_PROGRESS, WON, LOST }

src/main/java/Board.java:
- public final class Board {
  public Board();
  public void clear();
  public int[][] getGridCopy();
  public void setCell(int row, int col, int value);
  public MoveResult move(Direction dir);
  public boolean hasTileAtLeast(int value);
  public boolean hasAnyMoves();
}
Semantics:
- Board owns the authoritative 4x4 int grid. No external code may mutate it except through setCell().
- getGridCopy() returns a deep snapshot (new arrays). Callers must not mutate the returned arrays expecting to affect Board.
- setCell(row,col,value) performs bounds checks (0..3) and value validation: value == 0 or value is a positive power of two. Sets grid[row][col] accordingly.
- move(dir) processes each of the four lines (rows for LEFT/RIGHT, columns for UP/DOWN) independently:
  * Read exactly four values in movement order (LEFT: left->right; RIGHT: right->left; UP: top->bottom; DOWN: bottom->top).
  * Compact nonzero tiles preserving order.
  * Merge adjacent equal tiles at most once per adjacency (i.e., a tile participates in at most one merge). When merging two equal tiles x and x, produce 2x and add 2x to scoreGained.
  * After merging, compact again and fill with zeros to length four.
  * Write back exactly four results to the grid in the same line and movement orientation.
  * Overall changed flag is true if any cell differs from its previous value anywhere on the grid.
- hasTileAtLeast(value) returns true if any cell >= value.
- hasAnyMoves() returns true if any cell is zero, or any horizontal or vertical adjacent pair is equal, implying at least one legal move remains.

src/main/java/Game.java:
- public final class Game {
  public Game(Board board, Spawner spawner);
  public void reset();
  public MoveResult move(Direction dir);
  public int getScore();
  public GameStatus getStatus();
  public int[][] getGridCopy();
}
Semantics:
- Constructor requires non-null Board and Spawner; initializes score to 0 and status to IN_PROGRESS.
- reset(): calls board.clear() and applies exactly two spawns, each obtained by spawner.nextSpawn() and applied via board.setCell(). Resets score to 0 and status to IN_PROGRESS.
- move(dir): calls board.move(dir) once, increments internal score by result.scoreGained(). If result.changed() is true, consumes exactly one Spawn from spawner and applies it via board.setCell(). After the move attempt (even if unchanged), updates status: WON iff board.hasTileAtLeast(2048); else LOST iff !board.hasAnyMoves(); else IN_PROGRESS. Returns the MoveResult from Board.
- getGridCopy() proxies board.getGridCopy().

src/main/java/Main.java:
- public final class Main { public static void main(String[] args); }
- Deterministic headless console demo: constructs SequenceSpawner.defaultSequence(), Board, Game; calls reset(); performs one move (e.g., Direction.LEFT); prints the 4x4 grid, current score, and status in a plain text format; exits.

Build & Test:
- pom.xml sets Java 11, includes JUnit Jupiter as test dependency, and a Surefire plugin version supporting JUnit 5. No external non-test dependencies.

Import/Dependency rules:
- Board is the sole owner of the grid. All mutations go through Board.setCell().
- Pure domain logic (Board, MoveResult, Direction, Spawner, SequenceSpawner, Spawn, GameStatus, Game) must not depend on environment-specific code (Main). Main depends on Game and related domain classes only.
- Tests use JUnit 5 (Jupiter) and reference only declared classes.

Determinism:
- SequenceSpawner consumes its sequence strictly in order for both reset() and subsequent spawns.
